ma:\n    Id: 行标识，仅用于预测对齐。训练集和测试集分别编号，ID 可能重叠，禁止据此关联标签。\n    SeriousDlqin2yrs: 二分类标签，1 表示两年内发生严重逾期，0 表示未发生；仅训练集包含。\n    RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines: 无担保循环信贷额度使用比例。\n    age: 年龄。\n    NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse: 过去两年逾期 30 至 59 天的次数。\n    DebtRatio: 债务支出与收入的比值。\n    MonthlyIncome: 月收入；可能缺失。\n    NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans: 在用信用账户及贷款数量。\n    NumberOfTimes90DaysLate: 过去两年逾期至少 90 天的次数。\n    NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines: 房地产贷款或授信数量。\n    NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse: 过去两年逾期 60 至 89 天的次数。\n    NumberOfDependents: 被赡养人数；可能缺失。\n\n\n## Runtime dataset mapping (relative to the active task input directory)\n- Labeled training data: train_data/train.csv\n- Unlabeled prediction data: predict_data/test.csv\nThese paths override source paths or example filenames in the business description.\nIn a coding notebook, read from ../input/data/ using these relative\npaths. This points to the evaluator\'s public split, not the\noriginal training source. Preserve prediction row identifiers and output format.\nDo not modify source files; extract archives and write generated files in the\nworking/public directories. Never read or copy hidden validation labels.\n</task_desc>\n<experiment>Hypothesis: A median-imputed LightGBM binary classifier will establish a reproducible CPU baseline with ROC-AUC materially above 0.5; this becomes the fallback champion for later rounds.\n\nParent result: None (first round).\n\nValidation comparison: Single measured ROC-AUC on the fixed 30000-row validation split provided as validation_data/ (unlabeled features only), scored against hidden labels by the evaluator. Predictions produced by predict_proba positive class, not thresholded.\n\nData loading: ../input/data/train_data/train.csv (120000 labeled rows, 10 features + SeriousDlqin2yrs, no Id needed for modeling but retained for reference), ../input/data/predict_data/test.csv (101503 rows, Id-keyed), ../input/data/validation_data/ (30000 unlabeled features — exact layout discovered at runtime by globbing for the CSV; Id column preserved).\n\nData-quality audit (printed, saved): per-column missingness, count of RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines > 1, delinquency columns == 96/98 sentinel counts, quantiles for DebtRatio/MonthlyIncome, duplicate feature-row count, target rate (~6.684%).\n\nFeature handling: Drop Id. Median-impute MonthlyIncome and NumberOfDependents (medians fit ONLY on the 120k train rows), no scaling. Features = the 9 remaining numeric columns.\n\nModel: lightgbm.LGBMClassifier(objective=\'binary\', num_leaves=31, learning_rate=0.05, n_estimators=600, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.9, random_state=42, n_jobs=4, metric=\'auc\'). Early stopping on an internal 15% stratified split of the 120k train rows (e.g. train_test_split(test_size=0.15, stratify=y, random_state=42)); the fixed validation labels are never used for any fitting/early-stopping decision. Report internal-train-split AUC and the fixed-validation ROC-AUC (output only probabilities; the evaluator computes the score).\n\nHardware: CPU only, n_jobs<=4, memory well under ~2GB, runtime target under ~120s.\n\nBudget: one LightGBM fit + preprocessing + inference on 30000 val + 101503 test rows.\n\nOutputs: predictions.csv (Id,Probability, 101503 rows, test.csv Id order, no index, two columns), validation_predictions.csv (Id,Probability, 30000 rows, as returned file path), artifacts: model.txt/pkl (LightGBM booster + imputer medians), audit_report.json, run_log.txt with measured AUC and pipeline description; README describing inference steps. Provide both file paths.</experiment>\n<code_outline>import os, glob, json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\nimport lightgbm as lgb\n\nSEED = 42\nTRAIN = "../input/data/train_data/train.csv"\nTEST  = "../input/data/predict_data/test.csv"\n\ndef find_val():\n    # validation_data/ may contain one CSV (features + Id)\n    cands = [p for p in glob.glob("../input/data/validation_data/*.csv")]\n    assert len(cands) >= 1, "no validation csv found"\n    return cands[0]\n\ntrain = pd.read_csv(TRAIN)\ntest  = pd.read_csv(TEST)\nval_path = find_val()\nval = pd.read_csv(val_path)\nprint("shapes", train.shape, test.shape, val.shape)\nassert "SeriousDlqin2yrs" in train.columns\nfeatures = [c for c in train.columns if c not in ("Id", "SeriousDlqin2yrs")]\nprint("features", features)\n\n# ---- audit ----\naudit = {}\naudit["n_train"] = int(len(train)); audit["pos_rate"] = float(train.SeriousDlqin2yrs.mean())\naudit["missing"] = train[features].isna().sum().to_dict()\naudit["ru_gt1"] = int((train.RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines > 1).sum())\nfor c in ["NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse","NumberOfTimes90DaysLate","NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse"]:\n    audit[f"{c}_sentinel_96_98"] = int(train[c].isin([96,98]).sum())\naudit["DebtRatio_q"] = train.DebtRatio.quantile([.5,.9,.99,.995]).to_dict()\naudit["MonthlyIncome_q"] = train.MonthlyIncome.quantile([.5,.9,.99,.995]).to_dict()\nprint(json.dumps({k:(str(v)) for k,v in audit.items()}, indent=2))\n\n# ---- impute (fit on train only) ----\nmedians = {c: float(train[c].median()) for c in ["MonthlyIncome","NumberOfDependents"]}\ndef prep(df):\n    X = df[features].copy()\n    for c, m in medians.items(): X[c] = X[c].fillna(m)\n    return X\nXtr_full = prep(train); Xte = prep(test); Xval = prep(val)\ny = train.SeriousDlqin2yrs.values\n\nXtr, Xho, ytr, yho = train_test_split(Xtr_full, y, test_size=0.15, stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\n\nmodel = lgb.LGBMClassifier(objective="binary", num_leaves=31, learning_rate=0.05,\n                           n_estimators=600, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.9,\n                           random_state=SEED, n_jobs=4, metric="auc")\nmodel.fit(Xtr, ytr, eval_set=[(Xho, yho)], eval_metric="auc",\n          callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(50, verbose=False), lgb.log_evaluation(0)])\nho_auc = roc_auc_score(yho, model.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1])\nprint("holdout AUC", ho_auc)\n\nval_prob = model.predict_proba(Xval)[:,1]\ntest_prob = model.predict_proba(Xte)[:,1]\nassert np.isfinite(val_prob).all() and val_prob.min()>=0 and val_prob.max()<=1\nassert np.isfinite(test_prob).all() and test_prob.min()>=0 and test_prob.max()<=1\n\n# outputs\npd.DataFrame({"Id": val["Id"].values, "Probability": val_prob}).to_csv("validation_predictions.csv", index=False)\nout = pd.DataFrame({"Id": test["Id"].values, "Probability": test_prob})\nassert len(out)==101503 and list(out.columns)==["Id","Probability"]\nout.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\n# artifacts\nmodel.booster_.save_model("lgbm_baseline.txt")\njson.dump({"medians":medians,"features":features,"holdout_auc":ho_auc,"audit":audit,\n           "params":{"num_leaves":31,"lr":0.05,"seed":SEED,"n_jobs":4}},\n          open("run_meta.json","w"), indent=2, default=str)\nprint("done")</code_outline>\n\nRead local data from ../input/data/. It contains the fixed public training split,\nunlabeled validation inputs in validation_data/, a sample validation prediction\nfile and the unlabeled business prediction data. Inspect their actual schemas.\n<data_preview>```\ninput/\n    data/\n        split_info.json (29 lines)\n        validation_sample_predictions.csv (30001 lines)\n        predict_data/\n            test.csv (101504 lines)\n        train_data/\n            train.csv (120001 lines)\n        validation_data/\n            validation_features.csv (30001 lines)\n            validation_sample_predictions.csv (30001 lines)\nworking/\n    coder.log (0 lines)\n    llm.log (0 lines)\n    best_prediction/\n```</data_preview>\n\nThe business task defines the target, primary metric, validation strategy, output\ncolumns, row identifiers and constraints. Use only supplied local data and parent\nartifacts. Do not download datasets, pretrained weights or predictions. Fit all\npreprocessing on training rows only; never read hidden validation labels, source\ntraining files