nfig. Seed = 42 global; bag seeds [42,7,123,2024,555]; `n_jobs=4`; CPU only.\n\n**Evidence (executed).**\n- Baseline single LGBM (leaves=31, lr=0.05, 19 raw feats): holdout AUC 0.86674 → fixed 0.8680.\n- FE single model: holdout 0.86683 → fixed 0.8685.\n- LGBM+LR rank blend (19 feats): holdout 0.86688 → fixed 0.8693.\n- Tuned leaves=15/lr=0.03 4-seed bag: holdout 0.86856 → fixed 0.8700.\n- 28-feature 4-seed bag: holdout 0.86840 → fixed 0.8702.\n- 3-way rank blend (19bag+28bag+LR, w≈0.5/0.45/0.05): holdout 0.86872 → fixed 0.8703.\n- **33-feature 5-seed bag: holdout 0.86825 → fixed 0.8705 (best).**\n\n**Changes from parent.** Parent was None (first round); established the initial baseline and iterated through feature engineering, model regularization, LR blending, and bagging.\n\n**Artifacts** (working dir): `predictions.csv` (101503 rows, test Id order, Id,Probability), `validation_predictions.csv` (30000 rows), `artifacts/lgbm_bag33_*.txt` (5 boosters, one per seed), `artifacts/run_meta_bag33.json` (features, medians, n_it, seeds, holdout AUC), `artifacts/run_log.txt` (all rounds).\n\n**Load the saved model:** reconstruct features via the `build()` function using the stored `features` and `medians` from `run_meta_bag33.json`, then for each booster `lgb.Booster(model_file=\'artifacts/lgbm_bag33_<seed>.txt\')` and average `predict()` positive probabilities across the 5 seeds.\n</description>\n<code>\n# Concise outline of best measured approach (33-feature, 5-seed LightGBM bag)\n1. Read train/test/validation CSV from ../input/data.\n2. build(df): median-impute MonthlyIncome & NumberOfDependents (medians from train);\n   cap delinquency sentinels 96/98 -> 20 with flag; clip utilization to 1.5 with gt1 flag;\n   add 33 engineered features (missing flags, ratios, log, delinq aggregates).\n3. y = SeriousDlqin2yrs; internal split train_test_split(test_size=0.15, stratify, seed=42).\n4. Probe LGBM(leaves=15, lr=0.03, reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9,\n   colsample_bytree=0.8) with early_stopping(100) -> n_it ~371.\n5. Bag 5 seeds [42,7,123,2024,555] on 15% holdout -> holdout AUC (~0.868).\n6. Refit the 5-seed bag on full 120k, average predict_proba over seeds for validation & test.\n7. Assert 30000 / 101503 rows, finite probabilities in [0,1], unique Ids.\n8. Write validation_predictions.csv and predictions.csv; save 5 boosters + run_meta JSON.\n</code>\n<suggestions>\n**Observed weaknesses / lessons (evidence-based):**\n- Holdout AUC and fixed-split metric diverge at the 0.868–0.871 margin (e.g., 3-way blend had higher holdout 0.86872 but lower fixed 0.8703 than the 33-feat bag whose holdout was 0.86825). Differences of ±0.0003 are within noise — chasing them risks overfitting the fixed split indirectly. Treat gains <0.0005 as inconclusive.\n- Adding raw feature breadth (28→33 features) lowered holdout AUC (0.86840→0.86825) yet raised fixed split (0.8702→0.8705) — feature addition is not monotonically helpful; tree models already capture most interactions.\n- Probability calibration was never checked (only ranking/AUC matters here, so acceptable for the metric, but not for downstream thresholding).\n- Duplicate feature rows (464) and heavy DebtRatio tail remain unaddressed; may add noise.\n\n**Prioritized next experiments (hypotheses to test, not yet measured):**\n1. **Wider seed bag / repeated CV** (e.g., 8–10 seeds) to reduce variance in the final probability — likely small, stable gain; monitor runtime (<300s cell cap).\n2. **Fixed-split vs holdout reconciliation**: use the same stratification ratio and larger internal holdout (20%) to better mirror the fixed split; re-select config by internal metric and cross-check that gains hold. Hypothesis: prior "improvements" partly tracked fixed-split noise.\n3. **CatBoost-free GOSS/DART LightGBM variant** and/or `is_unbalance`/scale_pos_weight — test whether imbalance handling helps AUC (usually minimal for AUC, but worth one controlled run).\n4. **Feature selection**: prune the 33 features to those with top gain importance ≥ threshold to test whether fewer, cleaner features recover the 0.86872 holdout while holding fixed split; risk of regression is moderate.\n5. **Monotonic constraints** on delinquency counts / utilization (credit-risk domain knowledge) — could improve generalization; not yet tested.\n\n**Do not**: rely on holdout deltas below 0.0005 as real signal; the fixed split stays authoritative but measured only by evaluator.\n</suggestions>', role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_specific_fields={})], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=1757, prompt_tokens=26162, total_tokens=27919, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetailsWrapper(audio_tokens=None, cache_write_tokens=None, cached_tokens=23680, image_tokens=None, text_tokens=None), prompt_cache_hit_tokens=23680, prompt_cache_miss_tokens=2482))
