erve test.csv Id order; never use Id as a feature.\n2. Feature handling (identical to champion, fit stats on 120k train only, medians stored):\n   - Median-impute MonthlyIncome and NumberOfDependents.\n   - Cap delinquency sentinel codes {96,98}→20 with a delinq_sentinel flag.\n   - Clip RevolvingUtilization to [0,1.5] with ru_gt1_flag.\n   - Build the 33 engineered features (missing flags, total_delinq, delinq_weighted, ru_x_delinq, debt_per_income, income_per_dependent/line, log_MonthlyIncome/DebtRatio, debt_per_line, has_delinq_any, age_x_delinq, re_loan_ratio, util_x_dti, debt_pressure, ru_over_lines, sev_delinq_rate). Id excluded.\n3. Model: LightGBM binary (objective=binary), num_leaves=15, learning_rate=0.03, reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9 (bagging_fraction), colsample_bytree=0.8, n_jobs=4, seed=42 global. n_estimators fixed ≈371 (from champion\'s internal early-stopping on a 15% stratified split of the 120k rows only, never the fixed validation).\n4. Bag: refit on full 120k with seeds [42,7,123,2024,555,13,99,314] (8 seeds), average predict_proba positive-class probability across seeds. Apply the SAME averaged ensemble to both the fixed validation features and the test features.\n5. Hardware: CPU only, n_jobs=4, CPU core limit 4. Budget: ~8 Boosters × ~371 trees × 33 features on 120k rows; well within the 300s/cell cap.\n6. Validation comparison: compute fixed-validation ROC-AUC with sklearn.metrics.roc_auc_score on the 30000-row validation predictions. Compare to 0.8705. Ship this model only if it beats or holds (≥0.8705 - noise); otherwise record as failed hypothesis and retain champion.\n7. Output: predictions.csv (101503 rows, test.csv Id order, exactly Id,Probability, no index, finite in [0,1]) and validation_predictions.csv (30000 rows, Id,Probability, unique Ids matching provided validation Id list, no extras). Integrity asserts: exact row counts, unique Ids, finite probs.\n8. Artifacts: 8 boosters (artifacts/lgbm_bag33_s8_<seed>.txt), run_meta JSON (features, medians, n_it=371, seeds, holdout AUC, measured fixed-validation AUC), predictions/validation CSVs, and an inference README documenting the exact pipeline. Save predictions and model from the same single ensemble — no full-data retrain for output files. Return both file paths.\n\nExpected impact: small positive or neutral; risk low since only the seed-bag width changes.</experiment>\n<code_outline>import os, json\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd\nimport lightgbm as lgb\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n\nSEED = 42\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\nBASE = \'../input/data\'\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f\'{BASE}/train_data/train.csv\')\ntest = pd.read_csv(f\'{BASE}/predict_data/test.csv\')\nval = pd.read_csv(f\'{BASE}/validation_data/validation_features.csv\')  # 30000 unlabeled rows\n\nassert \'SeriousDlqin2yrs\' in train.columns and len(train) == 120000\nassert len(test) == 101503\nassert \'Id\' not in [] and \'Id\' in test.columns\n\nTARGET = \'SeriousDlqin2yrs\'\ny = train[TARGET].values\n\ndef build(df, med_inc, med_dep):\n    d = df.copy()\n    d[\'MonthlyIncome\'] = d[\'MonthlyIncome\'].fillna(med_inc)\n    d[\'NumberOfDependents\'] = d[\'NumberOfDependents\'].fillna(med_dep)\n    d[\'inc_missing\'] = df[\'MonthlyIncome\'].isna().astype(int)\n    d[\'dep_missing\'] = df[\'NumberOfDependents\'].isna().astype(int)\n    # sentinel capping\n    delq_cols = [\'NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\n                 \'NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\n                 \'NumberOfTimes90DaysLate\']\n    d[\'delinq_sentinel\'] = (d[delq_cols] >= 96).any(axis=1).astype(int)\n    for c in delq_cols:\n        d[c] = np.where(d[c] >= 96, 20, d[c])\n    # utilization\n    d[\'ru_gt1_flag\'] = (d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'] > 1).astype(int)\n    d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'] = d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'].clip(0, 1.5)\n    # engineered\n    d[\'total_delinq\'] = d[delq_cols].sum(axis=1)\n    d[\'delinq_weighted\'] = (d[delq_cols[0]] + 2*d[delq_cols[1]] + 3*d[delq_cols[2]])\n    d[\'ru_x_delinq\'] = d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'] * (d[\'total_delinq\']+1)\n    d[\'debt_per_income\'] = d[\'DebtRatio\'] / (d[\'MonthlyIncome\']+1)\n    d[\'income_per_dependent\'] = d[\'MonthlyIncome\'] / (d[\'NumberOfDependents\']+1)\n    d[\'income_per_line\'] = d[\'MonthlyIncome\'] / (d[\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\']+1)\n    d[\'log_MonthlyIncome\'] = np.log1p(d[\'MonthlyIncome\'].clip(lower=0))\n    d[\'log_DebtRatio\'] = np.log1p(d[\'DebtRatio\'].clip(lower=0))\n    d[\'debt_per_line\'] = d[\'DebtRatio\'] / (d[\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\']+1)\n    d[\'has_delinq_any\'] = (d[\'total_delinq\'] > 0).astype(int)\n    d[\'age_x_delinq\'] = d[\'age\'] * (d[\'total_delinq\']+1)\n    d[\'re_loan_ratio\'] = d[\'NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines\'] / (d[\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\']+1)\n    d[\'util_x_dti\'] = d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'] * d[\'DebtRatio\']\n    d[\'debt_pressure\'] = d[\'DebtRatio\'] * (1 - d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'].clip(0,1))\n    d[\'ru_over_lines\'] = d[\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\'] / (d[\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\']+1)\n    d[\'sev_delinq_rate\'] = d[delq_cols[2]] / (d[\'total_delinq\']+1)\n    return d\n\nmed_inc = train[\'MonthlyIncome\'].median()   # 5390\nmed_dep = train[\'NumberOfDependents\'].median()  # 0\nXdf = build(train, med_inc, med_dep)\nVdf = build(val, med_inc, med_dep)\nTdf = build(test, med_inc, med_dep)\n\nID_COLS = [\'Id\', TARGET]\nfeats = [c for c in Xdf.columns if c not in ID_COLS]\nX = Xdf[feats].values; Xv = Vdf[feats].values; Xt = Tdf[feats].values\n\n# internal holdout to fix n_estimators (~371) - 15% of 120k only\nXtr, Xho, ytr, yho = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=0.15, random_state=SEED, stratify=y)\nprobe = lgb.LGBMClassifier(objective=\'binary\', num_leaves=15, learning_rate=0.03,\n    reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.8,\n    n_estimators=2000, n_jobs=4, random_state=SEED)\nprobe.fit(Xtr, ytr, eval_set=[(Xho, yho)], eval_metric=\'auc\',\n          callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(100, verbose=False)])\nn_it = probe.best_iteration_ or 371\nholdout_auc = roc_auc_score(yho, probe.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1])\nprint(\'n_it\', n_it, \'holdout\', holdout_auc)\n\nSEEDS = [42, 7, 123, 2024, 555, 13, 99, 314]\nval_preds = np.zeros(len(Xv)); test_preds = np.zeros(len(Xt))\nos.makedirs(\'artifacts\', exist_ok=True)\nfor s in SEEDS:\n    m = lgb.LGBMClassifier(objective=\'binary\', num_leaves=15, learning_rate=0.03,\n        reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.8,\n        n_estimators=n_it, n_jobs=4, random_state=s)\n    m.fit(X, y)\n    val_preds += m.predict_proba(Xv)[:,1]\n    test_preds += m.predict_proba(Xt)[:,1]\n    m.booster_.save_model(f\'artifacts/lgbm_bag33_s8_{s}.txt\')\nval_preds /= len(SEEDS); test_preds /= len(SEEDS)\n\nfixed_auc = roc_auc_score(pd.read_csv(f\'{BASE}/validation_data/validation_labels_hidden.csv\')[\'SeriousDlqin2yrs\'], val_preds) if os.path.exists(f\'{BASE}/validation_data/validation_labels_hidden.csv\') else None\n\n# Outputs\npd.DataFrame({\'Id\': val[\'Id\'].values, \'Probability\': np.clip(val_preds,0,1)}).to_csv(\n    \'validation_predictions.csv\', index=False)\npd.DataFrame({\'Id\': test[\'Id\'].values, \'Probability\': np.clip(test_preds,0,1)}).to_csv(\n    \'predictions.csv\', index=False)\n\n# Integrity asserts\nvp = pd.read_csv(\'validation_predictions.csv\'); pp = pd.read_csv(\'predictions.csv\')\nassert len(vp) == 30000 and vp[\'Id\'].is_unique\nassert len(pp) == 101503 and pp[\'Id\'].is_unique\nassert list(pp.columns) == [\'Id\',\'Probability\']\nassert np.isfinite(pp[\'Probability\']).all() and pp[\'Probability\'].between(0,1).all()\nassert np.isfinite(vp[\'Probability\']).all() and vp[\'Probability\'].between(0,1).all()\n\njson.dump({\'features\': feats, \'med_inc\': float(med_inc), \'med_dep\': float(med_dep),\n    \'n_it\': int(n_it), \'seeds\': SEEDS, \'holdout_auc\': float(holdout_auc),\n    \'fixed_validation_auc\': fixed_auc}, open(\'artifacts/run_meta_bag33_s8.json\',\'w\'), indent=2)\nprint(\'fixed_validation_auc\', fixed_auc)</code_outline>\n\nRead local data from ../input/data/. It contains the fixed public training split,\nunlabeled validation inputs in validation_data/, a sample validation prediction\nfile and the unlabeled business prediction data. Inspect their actual schemas.\n<data_preview>```\ninput/\n    data/\n        split_info.json (29 lines)\n        validation_sample_predictions.csv (30001 lines)\n        predict_data/\n            test.csv (101504 lines)\n        train_data/\n            train.csv (120001 lines)\n        validation_data/\n            validation_features.csv (30001 lines)\n            validation_sample_predictions.csv (30001 lines)\nworking/\n    best_code.py (100 lines)\n    coder.log (1035 lines)\n    experiment.json (7 lines)\n    llm.log (36 lines)\n    predictions.csv (101504 lines)\n    validation_predictions.csv (30001 lines)\n    artifacts/\n        README.md (4 lines)\n        lgbm_bag28_123.txt (7196 lines)\n        lgbm_bag28_2024.txt (7196 lines)\n        lgbm_bag28_42.txt (7197 lines)\n        lgbm_bag28_7.txt (7196 lines)\n        lgbm_bag33_123.txt (7221 lines)\n        lgbm_bag33_2024.txt (7220 lines)\n        lgbm_bag33_42.txt (7220 lines)\n        ... and 18 other files\n    best_prediction/\n        predictions.csv (101504 lines)```</data_preview>\n\nThe business task defines the target, primary metric, validation strategy, output\ncolumns, row identifiers and constraints. Use only supplied local data and parent\nartifacts. Do not download datasets, pretrained weights or predictions. Fit all\npreprocessing on training rows only; never read hidden validation labels, source\ntraining files outside ../input/data/, or the private evaluator workspace.\nThe validation split is fixed for all experiments; do not change it to improve scores.\nYou may create an internal training holdout for tuning without changing the fixed\nexternal validation inputs. Record seeds and avoid target leakage.\n\nStart with a working baseline, then change a small number of factors at a time.\nUse observed execution errors and measured validation scores to choose improvements.\nExplain gains and regressions; do not claim results that were not executed.\nWrite complete prediction outputs for both validation and the business prediction\nset in the same cell. The business output must be ./predictions.csv and\nmust preserve the task\'s identifiers, ordering and schema. Save model, preprocessing\nand inference instructions in the working directory as requested by the task.\nParent artifacts, when supplied, are copied into ./ and can be reused; outputs\nfrom other workers in the current round are unavailable. Check alignment before\ncombining any predictions from your own local experiments.\nParent files may include later trials: check checkpoint metadata against the\nparent\'s scored code before reuse; retrain if their provenance is uncertain.\n\nA persistent Jupyter session is used. Propose one cell at a time, inspect its output,\nrepair failures, and then refine the best measured method within the budget.\nCheck package availability before use; use packages installed in this environment.\n<execution_environment>\nLocal execution platform: Darwin; CPU logical cores: 8.\nSelected training device: cpu.\nUse CPU training. Do not require CUDA, NVIDIA tools, or an MPS accelerator.\nIn notebook code, os.environ[\'BIZMIND_DEVICE\'] identifies the selected backend. Respect CPU limits and scale batch/model sizes to available memory; no GPU memory reservation is provided.\nCPU core limit: 4; keep n_jobs and thread counts within it.\nMaximum time per code cell: 300 seconds.\n</execution_environment>\nUse torch.device(os.environ[\'BIZMIND_DEVICE\']) for PyTorch models and tensors.\nDo not hardcode .cuda(). On MPS/CPU do not require CUDA-only operations or packages.\nUse CPU for libraries without support for the detected accelerator and choose\nmodel and batch sizes that fit available memory.\n\n<completed_local_parent_code>import os, json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\nimport lightgbm as lgb\n\nSEED = 42\nos.environ.setdefault("OMP_NUM_THREADS", "4")\nBASE = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/train_data/train.csv")\ntest  = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/predict_data/test.csv")\nval   = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/validation_data/validation_features.csv")\n\ndelinq = ["NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse","NumberOfTimes90DaysLate","NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse"]\nimpute_cols = ["MonthlyIncome","NumberOfDependents"]\nmedians = {c: float(train[c].median()) for c in impute_cols}\n\ndef build(df):\n    X = df.copy()\n    X["MonthlyIncome_missing"] = X["MonthlyIncome"].isna().astype(int)\n    X["NumberOfDependents_missing"] = X["NumberOfDependents"].isna().astype(int)\n    X["delinq_sentinel"] = X[delinq].isin([96,98]).any(axis=1).astype(int)\n    for c in delinq:\n        X[c] = X[c].where(~X[c].isin([96,98]), 20)\n    ru = X["RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines"]\n    X["ru_clipped"] = ru.clip(0, 1.5)\n    X["ru_gt1_flag"] = (ru > 1).astype(int)\n    X["DebtRatio_is_income"] = (X["DebtRatio"] > 10).astype(int)\n    for c, m in medians.items():\n        X[c] = X[c].fillna(m)\n    X["total_delinq"] = X[delinq[0]] + X[delinq[1]] + X[delinq[2]]\n    X["income_per_dependent"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfDependents"] + 1.0)\n    X["debt_per_income"] = X["DebtRatio"] / (X["MonthlyIncome"] + 1.0)\n    X["log_MonthlyIncome"] = np.log1p(X["MonthlyIncome"].clip(lower=0))\n    X["log_DebtRatio"] = np.log1p(X["DebtRatio"].clip(lower=0))\n    X["delinq_weighted"] = (X[delinq[1]]*3 + X[delinq[2]]*2 + X[delinq[0]])\n    X["ru_x_delinq"] = X["ru_clipped"] * (1 + X["total_delinq"])\n    X["debt_per_line"] = X["DebtRatio"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["income_per_line"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["has_delinq_any"] = (X["total_delinq"] > 0).astype(int)\n    X["age_x_delinq"] = X["age"] * (1 + X["has_delinq_any"])\n    X["re_loan_ratio"] = X["NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    # new orthogonal signals\n    X["income_per_person"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfDependents"] + 1.0)\n    X["util_x_dti"] = X["ru_clipped"] * X["DebtRatio"]\n    X["debt_pressure"] = X["DebtRatio"] * X["MonthlyIncome"] / 1e3\n    X["ru_over_lines"] = X["ru_clipped"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["sev_delinq_rate"] = X["NumberOfTimes90DaysLate"] / (X["total_delinq"] + 1.0)\n    return X\n\nfeat = [\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\',\'age\',\'NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\n        \'DebtRatio\',\'MonthlyIncome\',\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\',\'NumberOfTimes90DaysLate\',\n        \'NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines\',\'NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\'NumberOfDependents\',\n        \'MonthlyIncome_missing\',\'NumberOfDependents_missing\',\'delinq_sentinel\',\'ru_clipped\',\'ru_gt1_flag\',\n        \'DebtRatio_is_income\',\'total_delinq\',\'income_per_dependent\',\'debt_per_income\',\n        \'log_MonthlyIncome\',\'log_DebtRatio\',\'delinq_weighted\',\'ru_x_delinq\',\'debt_per_line\',\n        \'income_per_line\',\'has_delinq_any\',\'age_x_delinq\',\'re_loan_ratio\',\n        \'income_per_person\',\'util_x_dti\',\'debt_pressure\',\'ru_over_lines\',\'sev_delinq_rate\']\n\nfull = build(train)[feat]; te = build(test)[feat]; va = build(val)[feat]\ny = train["SeriousDlqin2yrs"].values\nXtr, Xho, ytr, yho = train_test_split(full, y, test_size=0.15, stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\n\ndef make(seed, n_it):\n    return lgb.LGBMClassifier(objective="binary", num_leaves=15, learning_rate=0.03,\n                              n_estimators=n_it, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9,\n                              subsample_freq=1, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_lambda=1.0,\n                              random_state=seed, n_jobs=4, metric="auc", verbose=-1)\nprobe = make(SEED,1500); probe.fit(Xtr,ytr,eval_set=[(Xho,yho)],eval_metric="auc",\n    callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(100,verbose=False), lgb.log_evaluation(0)])\nn_it = max(120,int((probe.best_iteration_ or 300)*1.1))\nauc_probe = roc_auc_score(yho, probe.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1])\nprint(f"probe(33 feats) holdout AUC={auc_probe:.6f} iter={probe.best_iteration_} -> n_it={n_it} (prev best blend 0.86872)")\n\nseeds = [42,7,123,2024,555]\nho = np.zeros(len(Xho))\nfor sd in seeds:\n    m=make(sd,n_it); m.fit(Xtr,ytr); ho += m.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1]\nho/=len(seeds); auc_bag = roc_auc_score(yho,ho)\nprint(f"bag5(33 feats) holdout AUC={auc_bag:.6f}")\n\nvp=np.zeros(len(va)); tp=np.zeros(len(te)); bst=[]\nfor sd in seeds:\n    m=make(sd,n_it); m.fit(full,y)\n    vp+=m.predict_proba(va)[:,1]; tp+=m.predict_proba(te)[:,1]; bst.append(m.booster_)\nvp/=len(seeds); tp/=len(seeds)\nfor nm,p in [("val",vp),("test",tp)]:\n    assert np.isfinite(p).all() and p.min()>=0 and p.max()<=1, nm\n\nos.makedirs("artifacts", exist_ok=True)\npd.DataFrame({"Id":val["Id"].values,"Probability":vp}).to_csv("validation_predictions.csv", index=False)\npo = pd.DataFrame({"Id":test["Id"].values,"Probability":tp})\nassert len(po)==101503 and list(po.columns)==["Id","Probability"] and po["Id"].is_unique\npo.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\nfor i,b in enumerate(bst): b.save_model(f"artifacts/lgbm_bag33_{seeds[i]}.txt")\njson.dump({"auc_probe":auc_probe,"auc_bag":auc_bag,"n_it":n_it,"seeds":seeds,"features":feat,"medians":medians},\n          open("artifacts/run_meta_bag33.json","w"), indent=2)\nwith open("artifacts/run_log.txt","a") as f:\n    f.write(f"[BAG33] probe={auc_probe:.6f} bag5={auc_bag:.6f} n_it={n_it}\\n")\nprint("done rows:", len(val), len(po))</completed_local_parent_code>\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>Test the 8-seed bag hypothesis: refit the champion 33-feature LightGBM config on the full 120k rows with 8 seeds, average positive-class probabilities across seeds for both fixed validation and test, and write both complete outputs. Expected runtime ~2-3 min (8 boosters x ~300 trees x 33 features on 120k rows, CPU n_jobs=4). Output: 30000-row validation_predictions.csv and 101503-row predictions.csv plus artifacts; tests whether wider bagging changes measured fixed-validation ROC-AUC vs champion 0.8705.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\nimport lightgbm as lgb\n\nSEED = 42\nos.environ.setdefault("OMP_NUM_THREADS", "4")\nBASE = "../input/data"\ntrain = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/train_data/train.csv")\ntest  = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/predict_data/test.csv")\nval   = pd.read_csv(f"{BASE}/validation_data/validation_features.csv")\n\n# schema checks\nassert len(train) == 120000 and "SeriousDlqin2yrs" in train.columns\nassert len(test) == 101503 and "Id" in test.columns\nassert len(val) == 30000 and "Id" in val.columns\nassert "SeriousDlqin2yrs" not in test.columns and "SeriousDlqin2yrs" not in val.columns\nprint("shapes", train.shape, test.shape, val.shape)\n\ndelinq = ["NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse","NumberOfTimes90DaysLate","NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse"]\nimpute_cols = ["MonthlyIncome","NumberOfDependents"]\nmedians = {c: float(train[c].median()) for c in impute_cols}\n\ndef build(df):\n    X = df.copy()\n    X["MonthlyIncome_missing"] = X["MonthlyIncome"].isna().astype(int)\n    X["NumberOfDependents_missing"] = X["NumberOfDependents"].isna().astype(int)\n    X["delinq_sentinel"] = X[delinq].isin([96,98]).any(axis=1).astype(int)\n    for c in delinq:\n        X[c] = X[c].where(~X[c].isin([96,98]), 20)\n    ru = X["RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines"]\n    X["ru_clipped"] = ru.clip(0, 1.5)\n    X["ru_gt1_flag"] = (ru > 1).astype(int)\n    X["DebtRatio_is_income"] = (X["DebtRatio"] > 10).astype(int)\n    for c, m in medians.items():\n        X[c] = X[c].fillna(m)\n    X["total_delinq"] = X[delinq[0]] + X[delinq[1]] + X[delinq[2]]\n    X["income_per_dependent"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfDependents"] + 1.0)\n    X["debt_per_income"] = X["DebtRatio"] / (X["MonthlyIncome"] + 1.0)\n    X["log_MonthlyIncome"] = np.log1p(X["MonthlyIncome"].clip(lower=0))\n    X["log_DebtRatio"] = np.log1p(X["DebtRatio"].clip(lower=0))\n    X["delinq_weighted"] = (X[delinq[1]]*3 + X[delinq[2]]*2 + X[delinq[0]])\n    X["ru_x_delinq"] = X["ru_clipped"] * (1 + X["total_delinq"])\n    X["debt_per_line"] = X["DebtRatio"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["income_per_line"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["has_delinq_any"] = (X["total_delinq"] > 0).astype(int)\n    X["age_x_delinq"] = X["age"] * (1 + X["has_delinq_any"])\n    X["re_loan_ratio"] = X["NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["income_per_person"] = X["MonthlyIncome"] / (X["NumberOfDependents"] + 1.0)\n    X["util_x_dti"] = X["ru_clipped"] * X["DebtRatio"]\n    X["debt_pressure"] = X["DebtRatio"] * X["MonthlyIncome"] / 1e3\n    X["ru_over_lines"] = X["ru_clipped"] / (X["NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans"] + 1.0)\n    X["sev_delinq_rate"] = X["NumberOfTimes90DaysLate"] / (X["total_delinq"] + 1.0)\n    return X\n\nfeat = [\'RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines\',\'age\',\'NumberOfTime30-59DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\n        \'DebtRatio\',\'MonthlyIncome\',\'NumberOfOpenCreditLinesAndLoans\',\'NumberOfTimes90DaysLate\',\n        \'NumberRealEstateLoansOrLines\',\'NumberOfTime60-89DaysPastDueNotWorse\',\'NumberOfDependents\',\n        \'MonthlyIncome_missing\',\'NumberOfDependents_missing\',\'delinq_sentinel\',\'ru_clipped\',\'ru_gt1_flag\',\n        \'DebtRatio_is_income\',\'total_delinq\',\'income_per_dependent\',\'debt_per_income\',\n        \'log_MonthlyIncome\',\'log_DebtRatio\',\'delinq_weighted\',\'ru_x_delinq\',\'debt_per_line\',\n        \'income_per_line\',\'has_delinq_any\',\'age_x_delinq\',\'re_loan_ratio\',\n        \'income_per_person\',\'util_x_dti\',\'debt_pressure\',\'ru_over_lines\',\'sev_delinq_rate\']\n\nfull = build(train)[feat]; te = build(test)[feat]; va = build(val)[feat]\ny = train["SeriousDlqin2yrs"].values\nXtr, Xho, ytr, yho = train_test_split(full, y, test_size=0.15, stratify=y, random_state=SEED)\n\ndef make(seed, n_it):\n    return lgb.LGBMClassifier(objective="binary", num_leaves=15, learning_rate=0.03,\n                              n_estimators=n_it, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9,\n                              subsample_freq=1, colsample_bytree=0.8, reg_lambda=1.0,\n                              random_state=seed, n_jobs=4, metric="auc", verbose=-1)\nprobe = make(SEED,1500); probe.fit(Xtr,ytr,eval_set=[(Xho,yho)],eval_metric="auc",\n    callbacks=[lgb.early_stopping(100,verbose=False), lgb.log_evaluation(0)])\nn_it = max(120,int((probe.best_iteration_ or 300)*1.1))\nauc_probe = roc_auc_score(yho, probe.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1])\nprint(f"probe(33 feats) holdout AUC={auc_probe:.6f} iter={probe.best_iteration_} -> n_it={n_it}")\n\nseeds = [42,7,123,2024,555,13,99,314]\nho = np.zeros(len(Xho))\nfor sd in seeds:\n    m=make(sd,n_it); m.fit(Xtr,ytr); ho += m.predict_proba(Xho)[:,1]\nho/=len(seeds); auc_bag = roc_auc_score(yho,ho)\nprint(f"bag8(33 feats) holdout AUC={auc_bag:.6f}")\n\nvp=np.zeros(len(va)); tp=np.zeros(len(te)); bst=[]\nfor sd in seeds:\n    m=make(sd,n_it); m.fit(full,y)\n    vp+=m.predict_proba(va)[:,1]; tp+=m.predict_proba(te)[:,1]; bst.append(m.booster_)\nvp/=len(seeds); tp/=len(seeds)\nvp=np.clip(vp,0,1); tp=np.clip(tp,0,1)\nfor nm,p in [("val",vp),("test",tp)]:\n    assert np.isfinite(p).all() and p.min()>=0 and p.max()<=1, nm\n\nos.makedirs("artifacts", exist_ok=True)\nvout = pd.DataFrame({"Id":val["Id"].values,"Probability":vp})\nvout.to_csv("validation_predictions.csv", index=False)\npo = pd.DataFrame({"Id":test["Id"].values,"Probability":tp})\nassert len(po)==101503 and list(po.columns)==["Id","Probability"] and po["Id"].is_unique\npo.to_csv("predictions.csv", index=False)\n\n# integrity\nassert len(vout)==30000 and vout["Id"].is_unique and set(vout["Id"])==set(val["Id"])\nassert len(po)==101503 and list(po["Id"].values)==list(test["Id"].values)\n\nfor i,b in enumerate(bst): b.save_model(f"artifacts/lgbm_bag33_s8_{seeds[i]}.txt")\njson.dump({"auc_probe":auc_probe,"auc_bag":auc_bag,"n_it":n_it,"seeds":seeds,"features":feat,"medians":medians},\n          open("artifacts/run_meta_bag33_s8.json","w"), indent=2)\nwith open("artifacts/README.md","w") as f:\n    f.write("Pipeline: build() median-imputes MonthlyIncome/NumberOfDependents (train medians), "\n            "caps delinq sentinels {96,98}->20 with flag, clips RU to [0,1.5], builds 33 features. "\n            f"LightGBM binary num_leaves=15 lr=0.03 subsample=0.9 colsample=0.8 reg_lambda=1.0 min_child_samples=40 n_it={n_it}. "\n            f"8-seed bag {seeds} averaged probs. Inference: apply build() with medians, average predict_proba[:,1].\\n")\nprint("done rows:", len(vout), len(po))</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>validation_predictions.csv</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>predictions.csv</prediction_file>'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Execution time: 18.49 seconds; success: True.\n<output>shapes (120000, 12) (101503, 11) (30000, 11)\nprobe(33 feats) holdout AUC=0.868041 iter=338 -> n_it=371\nbag8(33 feats) holdout AUC=0.868178\ndone rows: 30000 101503</output>\n<error></error>\nUse this evidence to repair failures or test the next controlled improvement.\n\nMeasured fixed-split validation metric: Metric↑(0.8705). Best so far: Metric↑(0.8705).\n\nRespond with exactly one executable notebook cell, using these tags:\n<goal>Hypothesis, expected runtime, expected output and how it tests the hypothesis</goal>\n<code>Python code for the next cell, without Markdown fences</code>\n<validation_prediction_file>Relative file path for complete validation predictions, or None</validation_prediction_file>\n<prediction_file>Relative file path for complete business prediction output, or None</prediction_file>\nBoth file tags must be None unless this cell writes BOTH complete outputs.\nDo not report an estimated score: the independent local evaluator measures it.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '<goal>Hypothesis: adding a small, well-regularized seed-diverse bag of a second model family (regularized logistic regression on a rank/quantile-transformed subset of the same 33 features) blended at a fixed weight with the 8-seed LightGBM ensemble will improve fixed-validation ROC-AUC by diversifying errors, subject to the 0.0005 noise threshold. We keep the current 8-seed LGBM as-is and add an LR branch fit only on the 120k train rows; blend weight chosen on the internal 15% holdout (never the fixed validation). Expected runtime ~60-90s. Writes both complete outputs; tests whether a diverse linear model can lift the ensemble.</goal>\n<code>import os, json, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import QuantileTransfor