d or matched — the linear/rank blend was rejected by the internal-holdout gate (best_w=0 because LR holdout 0.8595 << LGBM 0.8682).\n\nArtifacts (in working/artifacts/): run_meta_bag33_s12.json (best 12-seed run: n_it=371, seeds, feature list, medians), run_meta_bag33_s24.json, plus per-seed boosters lgbm_bag33_s8_<seed>.txt written in the 8-seed run. The README documents the exact inference pipeline: apply build() with the stored train medians, then average predict_proba[:,1] over the seed bag. Since the 12-seed run did not persist individual boosters, either rerun the 12-seed cell to regenerate boosters, or refit one booster per seed and average; predictions and models come from the same single ensemble (no full-data retrain for the output files). Predictions: working/validation_predictions.csv (30000 rows, Id+Probability, unique IDs matching the fixed validation set) and working/predictions.csv (101503 rows, test.csv Id order, Id+Probability, finite in [0,1]).\n</description>\n<code>\nBest measured approach (12-seed champion bag):\n1. Read ../input/data/train_data/train.csv (120k), predict_data/test.csv (101503), validation_data/validation_features.csv (30000).\n2. medians = train medians of MonthlyIncome & NumberOfDependents.\n3. build(df): missing flags, delinq sentinel {96,98}->20 + flag, RU clip [0,1.5] + ru_gt1_flag, DebtRatio_is_income, medians fill, then 33 engineered features (total_delinq, income_per_*, debt_per_*, logs, delinq_weighted, ru_x_delinq, has_delinq_any, age_x_delinq, re_loan_ratio, util_x_dti, debt_pressure, ru_over_lines, sev_delinq_rate).\n4. LGBM binary, num_leaves=15, lr=0.03, n_it=371, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9/freq=1, colsample=0.8, reg_lambda=1.0, n_jobs=4; fit on full 120k.\n5. seeds=[42,7,123,2024,555,13,99,314,101,777,222,999]; average predict_proba[:,1] over the 12 boosters for validation & test.\n6. clip [0,1]; assert row counts/unique Ids/Id order; write validation_predictions.csv and predictions.csv; save run_meta JSON + README.\n</code>\n<suggestions>\nEvidence:\n- Best measured fixed-valid ROC-AUC = 0.8706 (12-seed bag), up only +0.0001 vs parent 0.8705 — within noise. 24-seed bag did not exceed it (bag width saturated).\n- Internal 15% holdout is noisy: 36-feature slog variant improved holdout (0.86834 vs 0.86818) but regressed fixed validation (0.8704). Do not trust small holdout deltas.\n- LR (QuantileTransformer + LogisticRegression) reached only 0.8595 holdout — too weak to blend; linear diversity rejected by gate.\n- Deep-lite (num_leaves=31) holdout 0.867860 < champion 0.868245 — deeper trees hurt on this data.\n- Variant B (num_leaves=8) holdout 0.870463 > A holdout but tied at 0.8706 on fixed validation — noise, no real gain.\n\nHypotheses for next round (not yet tested):\n1. Cross-validated bag: run light 3-fold CV on the 120k only to derive a more stable n_it, then 12-seed bag at that n_it — may reduce the holdout-noise variance seen at 202/371 tree counts.\n2. Feature selection via LGBM gain importance on a 20% internal split (top-20 features), then 12-seed bag — low-cost check that removing useless features helps or not.\n3. Small hyperparameter probe localized around champion (e.g., min_child_samples in {30,40,60}, colsample in {0.7,0.8}) with 3-seed bags on internal holdout, ship only if holdout improves ≥0.0005.\n4. Avoid re-tuning n_it per experiment since it introduces drift (the 36-feat run picked 202 trees and regressed). Freeze n_it=371 for fair comparisons.\n5. Accept 0.8706 as near-saturated for this feature set; remaining headroom likely requires new signal (e.g., ratio of income to debt across loans) rather than more ensemble width.\n</suggestions>", role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_specific_fields={})], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=1582, prompt_tokens=41351, total_tokens=42933, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetailsWrapper(audio_tokens=None, cache_write_